@startuml
title Opening and rendering a highlighted file (T3)

actor User
participant "App::open_or_focus_tab" as Open
participant "ide_core::syntax_for_path" as SFP
participant "ide_core::Buffer" as Buffer
participant "ui::render_editor" as Render
participant "ui::styled_line" as Styled
participant "TextBuffer::tokens_in_lines" as Tokens

User -> Open: Enter on main.rs (not yet open)
Open -> Buffer: Buffer::open(path)
Buffer --> Open: Ok(buffer)
Open -> SFP: syntax_for_path(path)
SFP --> Open: Some(&RUST)
Open -> Buffer: buffer.set_syntax(Some(&RUST))
note right of Buffer
  Retokenizes from scratch.
  Does NOT mark the buffer dirty.
end note
Open -> Open: push OpenBuffer, active_tab = Some(idx)

User -> Render: (next frame)
Render -> Render: visible_start..visible_end =\nbuf.scroll..buf.scroll+text_area.height
loop for each line in visible_start..visible_end
  Render -> Styled: styled_line(text_buffer, line)
  Styled -> Tokens: tokens_in_lines(line..line+1)
  Tokens --> Styled: tokens overlapping this line\n(may extend past line_end)
  Styled -> Styled: clamp each token to\n[line_start, line_end]
  Styled --> Render: styled Line (colored spans)
end
Render -> Render: Paragraph::new(lines)\n(no .scroll() -- already the visible slice)

User -> Open: types a character
Open -> Buffer: text_buffer_mut().type_text(...)
note right of Buffer
  TextBuffer::apply retokenizes only
  the affected line span -- no
  explicit re-highlight call needed.
end note
@enduml
